<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madurai Sultanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1335">1335</a>–<a href="/years/1378">1378</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Sultanate of Madurai, Ma'bar Sultanate</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Madurai Sultanate was a Muslim kingdom in the southern Tamil country, founded in 1335 when the governor Jalal-ud-din Ahsan Khan rebelled against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi-sultanate">Delhi Sultanate</a>. Its sultans killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoysala-empire">Hoysala</a> king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/veera-ballala-iii">Veera Ballala III</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tiruchirappalli">Tiruchirappalli</a> in 1343. Weakened by internal strife, it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kumara-kampana">Kumara Kampana</a> of Vijayanagara in 1378.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madurai-sultanate.jpg" alt="Madurai Sultanate" width="320" height="482" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Venu62 at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Thanjavur_temple.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
